96
00:05:26,880 --> 00:05:28,630
This is me at my very best...

97
00:05:29,000 --> 00:05:30,630
for right now, anyway.

98
00:05:32,130 --> 00:05:33,000
Say, Allen?

99
00:05:33,250 --> 00:05:34,000
Yes?

100
00:05:34,380 --> 00:05:36,290
Will you duel me with no holds barred?

101
00:05:37,540 --> 00:05:39,080
He didn't even need to ask.

102
00:05:39,710 --> 00:05:41,920
I'm out to win this year! Maximum effort!

103
00:05:44,580 --> 00:05:45,380
Thank you.

104
00:05:46,500 --> 00:05:47,210
Begin!

105
00:05:48,830 --> 00:05:50,580
I'm twice as fast as last year!

106
00:05:51,130 --> 00:05:52,250
And I'm going straight for the win!

107
00:05:59,580 --> 00:06:02,330
Why can't I land a hit?
I should be faster than him!

108
00:06:04,710 --> 00:06:06,500
Is he just reading all my moves?

109
00:06:10,000 --> 00:06:12,040
Dammit! It's my Sword Mastery skill!

110
00:06:12,460 --> 00:06:14,250
The level is too low!

111
00:06:17,500 --> 00:06:19,000
He still hits like a truck!

112
00:06:20,040 --> 00:06:20,670
Crap!

113
00:06:24,330 --> 00:06:25,210
The duel is over!

114
00:06:27,290 --> 00:06:28,290
I lost...

115
00:06:29,420 --> 00:06:31,580
I couldn't throw him off balance,
even with my superior speed.

116
00:06:32,170 --> 00:06:33,290
Did I need a bigger agility boost?

117
00:06:33,710 --> 00:06:37,830
No, he already overpowers me, so lowering
my attack stat would just make things worse...

118
00:06:38,250 --> 00:06:40,330
The Granvelle huntsman doesn't disappoint.

119
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,500
You had me sweating there.

120
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:45,040
Right. Thank you for the...

121
00:06:48,290 --> 00:06:49,040
Mihai.

122
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,790
You've put in hard work at the Academy
over the past three years.

123
00:06:53,330 --> 00:06:55,170
It's clear from how skillful you've become.

124
00:06:55,920 --> 00:06:58,380
Thank you, Father.

125
00:06:59,790 --> 00:07:01,960
You're pretty tough, Allen!

126
00:07:02,250 --> 00:07:04,920
Still no match for my brother, though.

127
00:07:04,920 --> 00:07:06,330
Who are you to talk?

128
00:07:06,750 --> 00:07:10,170
Oh, hey! You should have Mihai
start giving you lessons now that he's back.

129
00:07:10,250 --> 00:07:12,500
I would love to learn from him!

130
00:07:12,500 --> 00:07:14,830
Oh, let me join in, too!

131
00:07:15,250 --> 00:07:16,630
Cecil, Thomas.

132
00:07:16,960 --> 00:07:18,460
I need to speak with you two.

133
00:07:19,040 --> 00:07:20,630
What is it, Elder Brother?

134
00:07:21,460 --> 00:07:24,830
I must leave to undertake the Noble's Duty.

135
00:07:25,420 --> 00:07:27,170
I won't be coming home anytime soon.

136
00:07:27,500 --> 00:07:28,250
Huh?

137
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:31,580
I'm sorry. I know this comes as a surprise.

138
00:07:31,790 --> 00:07:34,040
Hold on. What kind of duty is it?

139
00:07:34,040 --> 00:07:35,670
I'm afraid I can't say...

140
00:07:35,670 --> 00:07:37,290
When do you have to leave?

141
00:07:37,670 --> 00:07:38,670
Tomorrow.

142
00:07:40,750 --> 00:07:41,960
Father?

143
00:07:46,250 --> 00:07:49,710
But I was so excited to have you home again...

144
00:07:50,040 --> 00:07:53,380
Don't fret. I'll be back in three years.

145
00:07:53,710 --> 00:07:54,750
Three years?!

146
00:07:55,830 --> 00:07:57,040
It takes that long?

147
00:07:57,750 --> 00:07:58,670
Cecil...

148
00:07:58,880 --> 00:08:00,460
Don't cry.

149
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,250
I see.

150
00:08:02,630 --> 00:08:08,750
It's such a shame, Baron Granvelle.
Two of your three kids got saddled with a talent.

151
00:08:08,750 --> 00:08:11,920
I seem to recall your eldest son
also had a talent, Viscount!

152
00:08:12,380 --> 00:08:16,000
You know how it goes.
We must fulfill the Noble's Duty.

153
00:08:16,790 --> 00:08:20,630
The baron knew this would happen all along.

154
00:08:21,500 --> 00:08:23,580
The Noble's Duty, huh?

155
00:08:24,210 --> 00:08:25,830
Sounds ominous as hell.

156
00:08:30,540 --> 00:08:33,460
I'll be waiting for you
to come back, Elder Brother.

157
00:08:33,790 --> 00:08:36,460
Thanks. See you later, Cecil.

158
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:39,330
You're the pride of our family, son.

159
00:08:39,750 --> 00:08:42,710
Fulfill your duty and come back to us, okay?

160
00:08:43,830 --> 00:08:44,460
Right.

161
00:08:52,130 --> 00:08:55,290
Allen. Watch after Cecil for me.

162
00:08:56,250 --> 00:08:57,670
Keep her safe, okay?

163
00:08:58,500 --> 00:09:01,210
Huh? Uh, sure.

164
00:09:03,790 --> 00:09:07,380
Farewell. I'm off to uphold the Granvelle name.

165
00:09:09,040 --> 00:09:10,670
We'll miss you!

166
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,080
Don't forget about us!

167
00:09:11,000 --> 00:09:13,080
Felt like he was trembling.

168
00:09:13,080 --> 00:09:14,380
Was it just my imagination?

169
00:09:15,880 --> 00:09:18,750
