244
00:12:49,290 --> 00:12:51,920
And Teddy can't even get close enough to attack!

245
00:12:53,380 --> 00:12:54,710
Bron! Use Protec-

246
00:12:57,290 --> 00:12:58,580
Yikes!

247
00:12:58,710 --> 00:13:00,630
I'm in trouble! Bron's down!

248
00:13:02,670 --> 00:13:03,670
Teddy! Cover for me!

249
00:13:08,080 --> 00:13:09,710
Ow, that hurt...

250
00:13:10,130 --> 00:13:11,670
Gotta recover my HP.

251
00:13:14,630 --> 00:13:15,500
What now?

252
00:13:15,830 --> 00:13:19,500
How can I summon enough creatures to
overwhelm the boss while fending off those spells?

253
00:13:20,250 --> 00:13:21,830
I think I'm boned.

254
00:13:22,500 --> 00:13:24,380
I'll just have to call it quits.

255
00:13:24,380 --> 00:13:25,960
Having a rough go of it, are we?

256
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:37,040
THE HARDCORE GAMER DOMINATES

257
00:13:33,040 --> 00:13:37,040
IN ANOTHER WORLD WITH GARBAGE BALANCING

258
00:13:37,830 --> 00:13:39,290
Captain Zenof?!

259
00:13:40,000 --> 00:13:43,750
How the hell? The knights shouldn't be here
until tomorrow at the earliest!

260
00:13:44,290 --> 00:13:46,580
All the smoke prompted me to come take a look.

261
00:13:49,460 --> 00:13:50,710
Care to explain?

262
00:13:51,130 --> 00:13:54,250
Well, I was hoping to wipe out the orc borough...

263
00:13:54,960 --> 00:13:55,790
Hmm.

264
00:13:56,420 --> 00:13:58,130
Oh crap. He's seen everything!

265
00:13:58,130 --> 00:13:59,040
Come back, everybody!

266
00:14:04,630 --> 00:14:06,790
No comment on my summon creatures?

267
00:14:07,960 --> 00:14:10,130
I shall slay the Orc King.

268
00:14:10,710 --> 00:14:14,540
You handle the other riff-raff,
Vice-Captain Leibrand.

269
00:14:14,710 --> 00:14:15,920
Understood, Captain.

270
00:14:16,380 --> 00:14:18,000
The Vice-Captain is here, too?!

271
00:14:24,170 --> 00:14:27,790
I would've liked some more EXP,
but this is just as good.

272
00:14:28,250 --> 00:14:30,460
A front row seat to a battle of aces!

273
00:14:41,380 --> 00:14:42,250
Whoa!

274
00:14:42,250 --> 00:14:45,790
The captain earned a sobriquet from being
such a powerhouse on the battlefield.

275
00:14:46,670 --> 00:14:49,290
People call him: Zenof the War Demon.

276
00:14:57,960 --> 00:15:00,710
No way! He's parrying hits
from a monster twice his size!

277
00:15:06,040 --> 00:15:07,460
Magic orcs.

278
00:15:07,790 --> 00:15:09,380
That explains where the fire is coming from.

279
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,460
What is that? Something similar
to Krena's Extra Skill?

280
00:15:35,250 --> 00:15:37,630
He was aiming for the magic orcs all along!

281
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:48,580
The vice-captain is just as OP as the captain!

282
00:15:48,750 --> 00:15:51,830
How did he get his ass handed to him
by Krena that one time?!

283
00:15:54,920 --> 00:15:55,880
Captain Zenof!

284
00:16:14,920 --> 00:16:16,920
H-holy shit...!

285
00:16:17,380 --> 00:16:21,460
He took out a B-rank monster
in one fell swoop? Without an Extra Skill?!

286
00:16:27,750 --> 00:16:30,210
I didn't make it back home before nightfall.

287
00:16:30,540 --> 00:16:32,250
Bet I'm getting yelled at again.

288
00:16:33,130 --> 00:16:35,380
I had a sneaking suspicion, but...

289
00:16:35,880 --> 00:16:39,000
you're the one who took out
the goblin nests, aren't you?

290
00:16:40,380 --> 00:16:41,330
Yeah.

291
00:16:43,580 --> 00:16:46,960
Not long after you became
the Granvelle's manservant,

292
00:16:47,420 --> 00:16:50,880
I started hearing reports of monster carcasses
piling up outside the city.

293
00:16:51,420 --> 00:16:53,250
They had been stripped their magic stones.

294
00:16:54,170 --> 00:16:57,170
It wasn't very difficult to narrow down
who it could be,

295
00:16:57,500 --> 00:17:01,250
given that you single-handedly hunted a White Deer
and even competed on par with Master Mihai.

296
00:17:01,830 --> 00:17:03,460
So, the jig is up, huh?

297
00:17:04,330 --> 00:17:05,960
You have a talent.

298
00:17:06,830 --> 00:17:10,210
Those animals who were fighting
alongside you are part of it, right?

299
00:17:10,500 --> 00:17:13,580
Yep, that figures. My cover's totally blown.

300
00:17:14,670 --> 00:17:15,790
That's right.

301
00:17:17,210 --> 00:17:19,500
I'm not admitting to any more than that.

302
00:17:19,920 --> 00:17:22,460
There's no telling what kind of mess
it'll make if I say anything

303
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:24,830
about being on talking terms
with the God of Creation.

304
00:17:25,540 --> 00:17:28,330
The baron already knows
you have a talent, by the way.

305
00:17:29,250 --> 00:17:31,830
It's what motivated him
to promote you to Huntsman.

306
00:17:32,290 --> 00:17:33,670
I suppose that makes sense.

307
00:17:33,830 --> 00:17:37,000
It's unusual for a kid my age to be granted
so much freedom and responsibility.

308
00:17:39,290 --> 00:17:40,330
Let me wipe you down.

309
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:46,330
Listen, Allen. If you wish me
to keep what I saw today a secret,

310
00:17:46,460 --> 00:17:48,380
then I shall leave it out
of my report to the baron.

311
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:53,210
But in exchange, I want you to keep me informed
on the progress of your monster hunts.

312
00:17:53,880 --> 00:17:56,170
Our goals are one in the same, are they not?

313
00:17:56,580 --> 00:18:01,380
I shouldn't undercut the knights
just for the sake of farming more EXP.

314
00:18:02,130 --> 00:18:04,170
Right. As you wish.

315
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:06,250
I've gotta say...

316
00:18:06,830 --> 00:18:10,130
I'm shocked this guy is still kicking.

317
00:18:10,790 --> 00:18:15,420
I mean, he's covered in battle scars
that never went away even after a level up.

318
00:18:16,330 --> 00:18:19,290
2 WEEKS LATER

319
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:21,250
YOU HAVE EARNED 25,000 EXP.

320
00:18:19,290 --> 00:18:21,250
YOU HAVE DEFEATED 1 ORC KING.

321
00:18:20,250 --> 00:18:21,000
Sweet!

322
00:18:21,460 --> 00:18:24,920
Mission complete! I've got it down
to a science now.

323
00:18:25,250 --> 00:18:32,790
ORC BOROUGH

324
00:18:25,630 --> 00:18:28,380
First, I attack from all sides
with a team of 40 Teddys.

325
00:18:28,790 --> 00:18:32,250
This puts a big dent into the orc forces
and prevents them from getting into formation.

326
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:35,420
Then I have my team target
the magic orcs until they're all dead.

327
00:18:35,880 --> 00:18:37,420
It's a battle of numbers.

328
00:18:37,960 --> 00:18:42,670
So long as I don't get attacked,
I can keep throwing summons at them until I win.

329
00:18:43,130 --> 00:18:47,210
The total EXP I earn from
an orc borough is... 335,000!

330
00:18:47,380 --> 00:18:49,540
That's over seven times what I get
from a goblin one!

331
00:18:50,080 --> 00:18:52,710
Leverage a temporary failure
to achieve eventual success.

332
00:18:53,040 --> 00:18:54,830
That's the hardcore gamer way!

333
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:58,960
ALLEN: AGE 10

334
00:18:56,210 --> 00:18:58,960
SEPTEMBER

335
00:18:59,080 --> 00:19:01,250
We're honored to have you here.

336
00:19:01,580 --> 00:19:03,580
Good. Thank you for the warm welcome.

337
00:19:04,040 --> 00:19:05,710
A royal messenger, huh?

338
00:19:08,670 --> 00:19:11,130
May I ask what brings you here today?

339
00:19:11,540 --> 00:19:13,290
I came to deliver this.

340
00:19:18,880 --> 00:19:20,130
What am I looking at?

341
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:22,630
That is your son's diary.

342
00:19:23,040 --> 00:19:26,540
Everyone is expected to write
periodic entries while at the barracks.

343
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:34,170
Please be aware that your son carried out
his mission dutifully and has been laid to rest.

344
00:19:38,130 --> 00:19:40,080
That's not how this is supposed to go!

345
00:19:40,420 --> 00:19:42,630
How can such a thing happen in just six months?!

346
00:19:42,960 --> 00:19:46,250
You people knew Mihai
was fresh out of the academy!

347
00:19:46,580 --> 00:19:50,290
I can only assume you used him like fodder
because of our status as lower-ranking nobles!

348
00:19:50,290 --> 00:19:54,040
And is that a sentiment you wish for me
to share with the king?

349
00:19:56,170 --> 00:19:56,960
Oh, Mihai...

350
00:19:57,080 --> 00:19:58,210
Milady!

351
00:19:58,420 --> 00:20:01,920
If you'll excuse us,
we have other places to visit today.

352
00:20:01,920 --> 00:20:03,000
Farewell.

353
00:20:07,670 --> 00:20:09,790
I remember him acting strange that day...

354
00:20:10,460 --> 00:20:13,670
Allen. Watch after Cecil for me.

355
00:20:14,670 --> 00:20:15,960
Keep her safe, okay?

356
00:20:18,040 --> 00:20:20,750
Did he know he would die?!

357
00:20:22,250 --> 00:20:25,420
Father... what is going on?

358
00:20:26,580 --> 00:20:28,790
I need everyone else to clear the room first.

359
00:20:29,290 --> 00:20:30,790
Including you, Thomas.

360
00:20:31,040 --> 00:20:32,420
Huh? But why?!

361
00:20:32,420 --> 00:20:34,960
I want to know, too, Father!

362
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,500
Why only tell Cecil?

363
00:20:41,170 --> 00:20:42,670
Poor Master Mihai...

364
00:20:44,000 --> 00:20:47,290
What? Are you telling me
you knew Mihai was going to die?!

365
00:20:48,210 --> 00:20:51,170
It's part of a certain duty that we nobles
are expected to fulfill.

366
00:20:51,170 --> 00:20:55,920
And so what? The only reason
we're alive is to be killed for this duty?!

367
00:20:56,080 --> 00:20:57,210
It's not like that.

368
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:58,750
Listen...

369
00:20:59,880 --> 00:21:01,630
Hold on, Cecil!

370
00:21:10,580 --> 00:21:12,420
So there's just nothing they can do?

371
00:21:12,880 --> 00:21:17,380
Is there some catch to being a noble
that forces them to adhere to this deadly duty?

372
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:24,420
I hope that Lady Cecil is okay...

373
00:21:25,170 --> 00:21:27,460
She hasn't come out of her room since last night.

374
00:21:27,710 --> 00:21:33,250
As I recall, the baron's parents and elder brother
also passed away at fairly young ages.

375
00:21:34,130 --> 00:21:36,630
All because of this "Noble's Duty" thing.

376
00:21:37,500 --> 00:21:41,830
I don't get it. Losing your life at 15,
it's just too cruel...

377
00:21:44,080 --> 00:21:46,250
We need help! Lady Cecil is missing!

378
00:21:47,080 --> 00:21:48,540
Lady Cecil!

379
00:21:48,790 --> 00:21:49,960
Lady Cecil!

380
00:21:50,790 --> 00:21:53,000
Dammit. Some manservant I am!

381
00:21:55,710 --> 00:21:57,040
She climbed down from the window?!

382
00:21:57,960 --> 00:21:59,460
Have you found Cecil?

383
00:21:59,460 --> 00:22:01,210
She might have left the estate.

384
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:02,750
I'm going to look outside!

385
00:22:05,040 --> 00:22:07,000
I'll find her, no matter what!

386
00:22:07,380 --> 00:22:09,170
I just hope she doesn't do anything rash!

